WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.560
Shine light on the dorsal striatum of a mouse that carries no opsin at all.

2
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.060
Its firing rate falls, and it starts turning to one side.

3
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.940
Owen, Liu and Kreitzer reported that in wild-type mice.

4
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.560
So what does a light-on, light-off comparison show?

5
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.020
It compares light with no light, in animals that happen to carry an opsin.

6
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.660
A recording tells you that activity goes with a behaviour.

7
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.440
It cannot tell you whether the activity produces it.

8
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.240
So change the activity on purpose.

9
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.880
Drive the cells, and you ask whether their activity is sufficient.

10
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.540
Suppress them, and you ask whether it is necessary.

11
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.780
Both answers hold only for the cells you targeted, the time you illuminated, and the

12
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.780
assay you scored.

13
00:00:56.683 --> 00:01:00.123
The minimum design crosses construct with light.

14
00:01:01.203 --> 00:01:04.303
Opsin with light. Opsin without light.

15
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:06.903
Fluorophore only with light.

16
00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:09.643
Fluorophore only without light.

17
00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:12.963
The quantity you care about is the interaction.

18
00:01:13.763 --> 00:01:17.763
That is the extra effect of light in animals that carry the opsin.

19
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:24.677
A usable claim names the cells, the projection, the timing and the behaviour.

20
00:01:26.157 --> 00:01:31.117
Tye and colleagues lit basolateral amygdala terminals in the central amygdala, in

21
00:01:31.117 --> 00:01:32.217
freely moving mice.

22
00:01:33.397 --> 00:01:36.737
Activating those terminals reduced anxiety-related behaviour.

23
00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:42.797
But light there can also excite axons passing through, and drive the parent cell

24
00:01:42.797 --> 00:01:47.377
bodies. So they blocked glutamate receptors locally in the central amygdala.

25
00:01:47.377 --> 00:01:50.317
That abolished the light-induced reduction.

26
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.860
Now the arithmetic, with numbers invented for teaching.

27
00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:01.400
A pilot gives 60 seconds of avoidance with the opsin, and 48 with the fluorophore

28
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:06.480
alone, both lit. The pooled standard deviation is 12 seconds.

29
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.020
The difference divided by that spread is an effect size of 1.

30
00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:18.740
For 80% power and a two-sided alpha of 0.05, that needs 16 animals per group.

31
00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.940
But if the true effect is half as big, it needs 63.

32
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.740
Count animals, not trials.

33
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:34.300
Eight mice with 40 trials each are eight animals with trials nested inside them, not

34
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.960
320 independent observations.

35
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:43.540
And a small pilot overestimates its own effect, because the pilot that overshoots is

36
00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.540
the one followed up.

37
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.580
So power the study on the smallest effect you would care about.

38
00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.420
Control for the light, and size for the smaller effect.
